G1  FROM THE ACTION: C-H/K's Friedmann equation and local G (symbolic)
========================================================================================================
    Friedmann (vary N, set N = 1): (-16*pi*G*rho_0 + 9*H**2*a**3*c_2 + 6*H**2*a**3 - 2*Lambda*a**3)/(16*pi*G) = 0
    H^2 = 2*(8*pi*G*rho_0 + Lambda*a**3)/(3*a**3*(3*c_2 + 2))
    => G_cos = 2*G/(3*c_2 + 2);  L340 static block at C = 0 (det M(0) = -64*c_2*k**10*(alpha_c - 2)): psi/psi_N = -2/(alpha_c - 2)  => G_N = -2*G/(alpha_c - 2)
    G_cos/G_N = -(alpha_c - 2)/(3*c_2 + 2);   Frusciante & Benetti eq. (9) at xi = 1, eta = alpha_c, lambda = 1 + c_2: -(alpha_c - 2)/(3*c_2 + 2)
  [PASS] G1 C-H/K's FRW Hamiltonian constraint gives G_cos = G/(1 + 3c_2/2); its static block gives G_N = G/(1 - alpha_c/2); G_cos/G_N = (2 - alpha_c)/(2 + 3c_2) is exactly the published Horava-gravity relation at xi = 1
         measured: G_cos/G_N = -(alpha_c - 2)/(3*c_2 + 2)
         reading:  the published cosmological constraints on (lambda, eta) at xi = 1 apply to C-H/K's lambda-channel with lambda - 1 = c_2, eta = alpha_c

