G5  A LAMBDA-CHANNEL THAT VANISHES ON FRW: -c_2 (K - <K>_Sigma)^2 (symbolic)
========================================================================================================
    FRW with the subtracted term: H^2 = 8*pi*G*rho_0/(3*a**3) + Lambda/3;  G_cos = G;  G_cos/G_N = -(alpha_c - 2)/2
    leaf average of a k = 2 pi n/L mode on the closed leaf: <delta K> = 0  -> the k != 0 block is L340's, verbatim
    equivalently: -c_2 int N sqrt(h) K^2 + 2 c_2 <K>(t) dV/dt - c_2 <K>(t)^2 V_N(t): a global (sequestering-like) term,
    leaf-nonlocal in the same sense as C-H's heat kernel; well defined on C-H's closed leaves (T^3)
