VERDICT
========================================================================================================
  C-H/K's lambda-channel, at the strength L340 needs for phantom tracking (c_2 >= 7.3e-03), is excluded by Planck-era
  cosmology: on FRW the candidate IS low-energy Horava gravity with lambda - 1 = c_2 (G1), and the published fits cap
  c_2 at 1.2e-02 .. 1.2e-02 (95%, every dataset combination; G2).  A growth-only cross-check lands at the same
  order (G3).  Inside the cosmological ceiling the phantom still tracks galaxy bodies, but deep-MOND outskirts are
  amplified by up to 2% and fast ones are left behind (G4): KM2's 'below reach' becomes 'at KiDS
  precision'.  The conflict disappears if the lambda-term acts only on the leaf-inhomogeneous part of K (G5) -- a
  global term on C-H's closed leaves, offered as a construction.  Time 0 s.

